abstract: "A research project on where a lesson learned in a long human and AI collaboration should live so that the next model does not repeat the mistake: in a prompt, a tool, a check, retrieval, a gate, or judgment. Contains a consolidated sheet of one house's repeated mistakes, a first experiment with rules frozen before the run and its raw data, and draft rules for a second."
keywords: ["human-AI collaboration", "lessons learned", "preregistration", "tool use", "small language models", "evaluation"]
notes: "Status: a starting line. Two pilots only; no result is established."
